From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UebelAndre <github@uebelandre.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:45:02 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(server): single-threaded mode

`--single_threaded` runs the transport, the event loop and every request
handler on one thread: read a message, handle it, run the tasks that
produced inline, flush the replies, block on the next read. The task pool
with zero threads runs closures on the caller and queues their results on
the usual channel, and the debouncer forwards file ids when the loop pumps
it instead of waiting on a thread, so edits are analysed immediately.

This is the mode a WebAssembly (WASI preview 1) build has to use, since it
has no threads; it is a flag on the native binary so the mode can be
tested without one. `canonicalize` goes through a helper that will fall
back to lexical normalization where there is no `realpath`.
